00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.840
Well, the the the core argument of the book is&nbsp;
that Silicon Valley should come to the defense of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:11.120
the nation that made its rise possible. You know,&nbsp;
I came of age during a generation where there was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:16.640
so much talent, so much funding really flowing&nbsp;
to Silicon Valley. But to build the trivial and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:22.000
ephemeral, you know, the iPhones that are in all&nbsp;
of our pockets, it's a wondrous invention. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.840
changed our lives. You know, we use the apps. Um,&nbsp;
but is that the is that the best we can do? Is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.360
that the crowning achievement of our civilization?&nbsp;
Shouldn't we be directing more energy, more time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.720
more heart, more money to the things that&nbsp;
really will move the needle? You know, we're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:44.080
involved with counterterrorism, national security,&nbsp;
medical research, industrial production. You know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:49.600
how can we convince people to spend their effort&nbsp;
and resources, scarce as they are, to what really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:56.960
matters? Um, I would also say I think you know in&nbsp;
some ways we take for granted the relative period&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:04.160
of not peace but geopolitical stability. It's&nbsp;
September 2025 essentially 80 years since the last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:12.960
time a nuclear weapon was used in war in Japan of&nbsp;
August of 1945. You know, we read the headlines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:20.400
we feel the conflict, you know, horrors and&nbsp;
uh and tragedy across the world, but we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.760
essentially lived through a very remarkable&nbsp;
period of, I would argue, geopolitical stasis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:30.960
if not peace, some degree of stalemate. There has&nbsp;
not been a great powers conflict for near nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:36.480
